<title>BELGIUM: W. Europe new car sales down 1.9 pct yr/yr in May.</title>
<headline>W. Europe new car sales down 1.9 pct yr/yr in May.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car registrations in western Europe dropped 1.9 percent year-on-year in May to 1,151,900 units, the European Automobile Manufacturers' Association (ACEA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the first five months of 1997, registrations rose 0.3 percent to 5,855,100 cars.</p>
<p>The 15 members of the European Union, Switzerland, Norway and Liechtenstein are included in the figures.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
